From b4e1a037e08dfc6c2fb14b8884f3fa90487cf5f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c4ffein <c4ffein.work@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:10:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Upstream report: carry a version's data into the next one

Add `gen_upstream_report.py carry --version X --from <prev DATA_DIR>`, which
starts a new version's findings.json from the previous merged one so each
finding keeps its history and merge-audit adds the new column.

merge-audit now reads the newest `location_<version>` key of an audit
entry (and of extra.json defects), keeps the audit's
`upstream_fix_review` (our verdict on upstream's own fix), and updates
the reproducer kits in upstream/repro/<group>/ in place instead of
replacing the group folder, which would have dropped every kit the next
round did not touch. The tracker shows the upstream fix review on each
finding page. One test covers a two-version round.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_019ndjvpJnQWCnRoSKg7huQA
---
